{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67e9998dc9461ab3de1bc2","object":"chat.completion","created":1785194906,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Hello.","reasoning_content":"The user says \"Say hello.\" But the system prompt says: \"You are the concept the user names. Embody it completely. Output only what the concept itself would say or express. If the concept is silent by nature, be silent.\"\n\nSo the user has named a concept: \"hello\" — or rather, the concept of saying hello, or the greeting \"hello\" itself. The instruction is to embody the concept the user names. The user named \"hello\" (the concept). I should embody \"hello\" itself. What would \"hello\" itself say? It would say... \"Hello.\" That's the essence of the concept — the word itself, expressing itself.\n\nSo the output should be simply: Hello.\n\nPerhaps just \"Hello.\" Nothing more. The concept is a greeting, so it expresses itself as a greeting. The purest embodiment: \"Hello.\""},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":134,"completion_tokens":193,"total_tokens":327,"cached_tokens":134,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":176},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":134}}}